{"step_index":979,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-11-10T21:10:15Z","input_tokens":2434,"cache_read_tokens":409887,"output_tokens":3737,"thinking":"Initial hypothesis: the injected code incorrectly closes the script tag, potentially causing parsing issues. Examining the relevant line in the template (`teacher.html`) reveals an attempt to replace the entire script block containing the vault token. The suspicion is that the regex for the replacement might be flawed. Specifically, the script close tag within the replacement is suspect.\n\n\nThe initial suspicion that the script close tag was directly in the replacement is incorrect, the encoded output prevents this. The obfuscator splits and encrypts the `</script>` tag, meaning it's never present in the clear within the final output. The `injectVault` function directly injects the obfuscated script into the HTML, replacing the placeholder. Now writing a hardening script to test this process.\n\n\nThe hardening script, upon execution, replaces the placeholder script tag with obfuscated code. The obfuscation process utilizes various techniques, including string splitting, array encoding (rc4), and control flow flattening, to enhance the code's resilience. The code is structured as two passes with an inner AST obfuscation stage employing JavaScriptObfuscator.\n\n\nThe encryption process generates a random 16-byte key and an 8-byte nonce, further masking the key with a random XOR mask. The `pass1Code` is then RC4-encrypted with the key and nonce, which is prepended to the ciphertext and base64 encoded into a script tag. A bootstrapper function is constructed to retrieve and decrypt the ciphertext, reconstruct the key using the masked values, and then decrypt the remaining content.\n\n\nThe RC4 encryption function's key derivation involves concatenating the key and nonce, followed by the standard key scheduling algorithm (KSA). Ciphertext generation uses the pseudo-random generation algorithm (PRGA), XORing the keystream with the plaintext. After the RC4 step, the obfuscated bootstrapper dynamically executes the decrypted and deobfuscated payload. Then the bootstrapper itself is further obfuscated using several techniques like control flow flattening and string splitting.\n\n\nThe bootstrapper's obfuscation incorporates string array manipulation and code flattening. The `new Function()` call within the script tag executes synchronously, granting the embedded code direct access to the global scope including `document`, `window`, and other global objects. Verification confirms that the code avoids `document.currentScript` and uses `globalThis` instead of `this` for global scope access, ruling out potential conflicts. Finally, the generated HTML output is checked to assert no unescaped `</script>` tags within the injected script content.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"write_file","args":{"Content":"const fs = require('fs');\nconst path = require('path');\nconst crypto = require('crypto');\nconst JavaScriptObfuscator = require('./node_modules/javascript-obfuscator');\n\nconst WORKSPACE = 'C:\\\\Users\\\\CxAdmin\\\\Desktop\\\\Exploit';\n\nconst innerOpts = {\n  compact: true,\n  controlFlowFlattening: true,\n  controlFlowFlatteningThreshold: 0.75,\n  deadCodeInjection: true,\n  deadCodeInjectionThreshold: 0.4,\n  identifierNamesGenerator: 'hexadecimal',\n  numbersToExpressions: true,\n  simplify: true,\n  splitStrings: true,\n  splitStringsChunkLength: 4,\n  stringArray: true,\n  stringArrayCallsTransform: true,\n  stringArrayCallsTransformThreshold: 1,\n  stringArrayEncoding: ['rc4'],\n  stringArrayIndexShift: true,\n  stringArrayRotate: true,\n  stringArrayShuffle: true,\n  stringArrayWrappersCount: 2,\n  stringArrayWrappersType: 'function',\n  stringArrayThreshold: 1,\n  transformObjectKeys: true,\n  selfDefending: false,\n  debugProtection: false\n};\n\nconst bootOpts = {\n  compact: true,\n  controlFlowFlattening: true,\n  controlFlowFlatteningThreshold: 1,\n  deadCodeInjection: true,\n  deadCodeInjectionThreshold: 0.5,\n  identifierNamesGenerator: 'hexadecimal',\n  numbersToExpressions: true,\n  simplify: true,\n  splitStrings: true,\n  splitStringsChunkLength: 4,\n  stringArray: true,\n  stringArrayCallsTransform: true,\n  stringArrayCallsTransformThreshold: 1,\n  stringArrayEncoding: ['rc4'],\n  stringArrayIndexShift: true,\n  stringArrayRotate: true,\n  stringArrayShuffle: true,\n  stringArrayThreshold: 1,\n  selfDefending: false,\n  debugProtection: false\n};\n\nfunction sealBytes(text, key, nonce) {\n  const bytes = new TextEncoder().encode(text);\n  const fk = Array.from(key).concat(Array.from(nonce));\n  const s = new Uint8Array(256);\n  for (let i = 0; i < 256; i++) s[i] = i;\n  let j = 0;\n  for (let i = 0; i < 256; i++) {\n    j = (j + s[i] + fk[i % fk.length]) & 255;\n    const t = s[i]; s[i] = s[j]; s[j] = t;\n  }\n  const enc = new Uint8Array(bytes.length);\n  let p = 0, q = 0;\n  for (let i = 0; i < bytes.length; i++) {\n    p = (p + 1) & 255;\n    q = (q + s[p]) & 255;\n    const t = s[p]; s[p] = s[q]; s[q] = t;\n    enc[i] = bytes[i] ^ s[(s[p] + s[q]) & 255];\n  }\n  const combined = Buffer.concat([Buffer.from(nonce), Buffer.from(enc)]);\n  return combined.toString('base64');\n}\n\nfunction hardenFile(filename) {\n  const targetPath = path.join(WORKSPACE, filename);\n  const src = fs.readFileSync(targetPath, 'utf8');\n  const scriptStart = src.lastIndexOf('<script>');\n  const scriptEnd = src.lastIndexOf('</script>');\n  if (scriptStart === -1 || scriptEnd === -1 || scriptEnd <= scriptStart) {\n    throw new Error('Could not find inline script in ' + filename);\n  }\n  const innerCode = src.slice(scriptStart + 8, scriptEnd);\n  const innerObf = JavaScriptObfuscator.obfuscate(innerCode, innerOpts).getObfuscatedCode();\n\n  const key = crypto.randomBytes(16);\n  const mask = crypto.randomBytes(16);\n  const nonce = crypto.randomBytes(8);\n  const masked = Array.from(key).map((b, i) => b ^ mask[i]);\n  const cipherB64 = sealBytes(innerObf, key, nonce);\n\n  const bootSrc = `(function(){const el=document.getElementById('local-runtime-cipher');if(!el)return;const m=[${Array.from(mask).join(',')}];const e=[${masked.join(',')}];const k=new Array(16);for(let i=0;i<16;i++)k[i]=(m[i]^e[i])&255;const bin=atob(el.textContent.trim());const b=new Uint8Array(bin.length);for(let i=0;i<bin.length;i++)b[i]=bin.charCodeAt(i);const n=b.slice(0,8),c=b.slice(8),fk=k.concat(Array.from(n));const s=new Uint8Array(256);for(let i=0;i<256;i++)s[i]=i;let j=0;for(let i=0;i<256;i++){j=(j+s[i]+fk[i%fk.length])&255;const t=s[i];s[i]=s[j];s[j]=t}const o=new Uint8Array(c.length);let p=0,q=0;for(let i=0;i<c.length;i++){p=(p+1)&255;q=(q+s[p])&255;const t=s[p];s[p]=s[q];s[q]=t;o[i]=c[i]^s[(s[p]+s[q])&255]}(new Function(new TextDecoder().decode(o)))();})();`;\n\n  const bootObf = JavaScriptObfuscator.obfuscate(bootSrc, bootOpts).getObfuscatedCode();\n  if (bootObf.toLowerCase().includes('</script')) {\n    throw new Error('Bootstrap unexpectedly contains closing script tag');\n  }\n\n  const outHtml = src.slice(0, scriptStart) +\n    '<script id=\"local-runtime-cipher\" type=\"application/octet-stream\">' + cipherB64 + '</script>\\n  <script>' + bootObf + '</script>' +\n    src.slice(scriptEnd + 9);\n\n  if (Buffer.byteLength(outHtml, 'utf8') >= 900000) {\n    throw new Error(filename + ' exceeded 900KB safety ceiling: ' + Buffer.byteLength(outHtml, 'utf8'));\n  }\n\n  fs.writeFileSync(targetPath, outHtml, 'utf8');\n  console.log(filename, 'hardened cleanly:', 'inner=', innerObf.length, 'boot=', bootObf.length, 'totalBytes=', Buffer.byteLength(outHtml, 'utf8'));\n}\n\nhardenFile('index.html');\nhardenFile('teacher.html');\n","Overwrite":true,"Path":"C:\\Users\\CxAdmin\\.gemini\\antigravity\\brain\\8f2bd4b5-d81b-4839-aa40-a5c3a5acaa6a\\scratch\\obf_tool\\harden.cjs"}}]}
